--- a/src/training/README.md
+++ b/src/training/README.md
@@ -36,7 +36,7 @@ Both stages are a `Demo`. Show demonstrates the job on mock screens; Info explai
 
 ## Spots
 
-A spot is a button, tile or row with an id. Add `spot={SPOT.something}` to `Btn`, `Chip`, `Row` or `IconBtn`, or wrap a view in `<Spot id=...>`. Static ids live in `src/lib/trainingSpots.ts`. Grid tiles and cart lines get ids from the item (`grid.item:<id>`, `cart.line:<variantId>`). Other record spots: a page chip (`grid.page:<pageId>`), a part of the Keypad | Quick Menu | All products switch (`find.tab:<keypad|quick|all>`, while the whole switch is `find.tabs`), a product row on All products (`all.product:<productId>`), a size in the variation picker (`pick.variant:<variantId>`) and an item row in the Search window (`search.result:<variantId>`, a window spot). Payment: `pay.total` (the amount due), `pay.card` (Card), and, as window spots, `pay.retry` and `pay.other` (Try card again and Use another method in the Not approved window) and `receipt.none` (No receipt in the Receipt window), `receipt.qr`, `receipt.email`, `receipt.text`, `receipt.share` and `receipt.qr.back` (the other Receipt window buttons, window spots). In practice the Receipt window is given a made-up server address, so it offers the QR code, and Email, Text and Share only say what would have opened. `isWindowSpot` says which spots live in a window. `tests/trainingspots.test.ts` reads the source, so a module cannot name a spot that is not there.
